{
  "name": "identity-stability",
  "integration": "tenable-ot-security",
  "description": "The regression lock for the foreign id. Asset 0001 is the same physical controller as in the happy scenario after a readdress and a rename -- new IP, new MAC, new name, same Asset.id -- and its runZero id must still be exactly tenable-ot-security:<console host>:<uuid>, with no address or name folded in. Asset 0002 carries the SAME name and an adjacent address under a different uuid, so a name- or address-derived key would collapse the two into one asset; they must stay distinct. Asset 0003 has no name at all and only an address, proving the id does not depend on a name being present.\n\nThe namespace is asserted with $HOST rather than $BASE_HOST because the console host, not host:port, is the scope: one appliance reached on two ports is one appliance, and check_determinism re-runs this scenario on a new ephemeral port, so a port-bearing id would change between polls and duplicate the whole estate. Both the port-bearing spelling and the un-namespaced raw uuid are asserted absent.",
